It is easy to see that the right-hand side of this inequality is a monotonically increasing function growing faster than the left-hand side and verify that the inequality holds for  $x=1$  and  $x=2$  but not  $x=3,$  so it follows that  $x \le 2,$  concluding the proof of this lemma.  $\blacksquare$  

