By Angle Chasing, we can say that  $B'CHA$  is a parallelogram. Notice that  $B',F, H$  are collinear. So, we can get  $MN || BC$  and  $HONM$  is cyclic quadrilateral.

By doing some more angle chasing, we can  get  $\angle KHO=\angle HOM$ , then  $\angle HOM=\angle HNM$ . Now, since  $MN|| BC$ , we get  $\angle HNM=\angle HCB=90^{\circ}-\angle B=\angle OAK$ . Hence, we can say that  $HOKA$  is a cyclic quadrilateral. The last two results are the properties in Pedal Triangle. Hence, we get  $OH\perp AG$  and then  $HO||MN \implies HO||MN||BC$ .

Lastly, we can say that  $\Delta KHN$  and  $\Delta B'HC$  are isosceles triangles and hence  $B'KNC$  is an isosceles trapezium. $\therefore B'N=FC, FC=\frac{1}{2} \implies B'N=\frac{1}{2}. \qquad \blacksquare$

