solution_md:
\[ Solution \]
Let the points  $A$ , $P$  and  $B$  be  $(t,f(t))$ , $(\sqrt \frac{f(t)}{2},f(t))$  and  $(\sqrt \frac{f(t)}{2}, \frac{f(t)}{2})$ .
Let us denote area by  $[\ ]$ .
So, \[[OAP]=[OAT]+[APST]-[OPS]\] $=\int^t_0 f(x)\,dx+f(t)(\sqrt \frac{f(t)}{2}-t)-\int^{\sqrt \frac{f(t)}{2}}_0 2x^2\,dx$ And , \[[OBP]=[OPS]-[OBS]\] $=\int^{\sqrt \frac{f(t)}{2}}_0 2x^2\,dx - \int^{\sqrt \frac{f(t)}{2}}_0 x^2\,dx$ As we have  $[OAP]=[OBP]$ Putting the values and simplifying, we get :- $\int^t_0 f(x)\,dx + f(t)(\sqrt \frac{f(t)}{2} - t) - (\frac{f(t)}{2})^{\frac{3}{2}}=0$ By arranging terms and differentiating , we get :- $f(t)+\frac{3}{4\sqrt{2}}\sqrt{f(t)}f'(t) - f(t) - tf'(t)=0$ After some cancellations , we get :- ${\sqrt{f(t)}=\frac{4\sqrt{2}t}{3}}$ Hence ,  $f(x)=\frac{32}{9}x^2$ .

